1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:05,177
This love in my heart,
it will burn on forever!

2
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:09,037
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop!

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,177
No matter where you
are, nothing is too far!

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,877
With our everlasting bones,
we'll reach it, we are home!

5
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:22,877
I'm so

6
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:23,917
truly grateful!

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,800
I ran into you on that day so long ago!

8
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,397
We laughed every moment
with tears in our eyes!

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,880
Till we knew we weren't alone!

10
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:41,820
The blowing wind came in
and joined us on our way!

11
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,097
And with it I know we'll rise!

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,797
We'll be flying up high!

13
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,920
Why, tell me why are you giving up?

14
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:56,160
Why, tell me why you wanna fight alone?

15
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,620
Hey, what kind of future
do you think you have?

16
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,197
Your dream is already in your hands.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,937
This love in my heart,
it will burn off forever.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:10,757
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,897
I don't matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

20
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:16,457
With our everlasting
plans, we'll reach it.

21
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:20,537
We are home from the horizon
out on the edge of the world.

22
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,497
If there is a place that
I want to take you to?

23
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,897
Let's head for it then!

24
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,540
But as for the way we already know.

25
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,620
We promised it long ago.

26
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:45,317
You scream by your voice.

27
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,257
That can't break through the silence.

28
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:48,817
Feeling defeated.

29
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,037
It crushes your helpless heart.

30
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,697
I've got your back, I swear.

31
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,177
I'll always be here.

32
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:58,100
Let's put our fate within
this light under the sun.

33
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,880
Can you close your eyes and
just listen to my voice?

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,897
Let's find the answer together.

35
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,597
I'm telling you in our path.

36
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,617
I trust that it will lead us.

37
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,517
To another sea untarded.

38
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,417
Cause now we are home.

39
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,197
On the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

40
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:19,197
There is a place that
I want to take you to.

41
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,697
Let's head for it then.

42
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:24,260
But after the way, we already know.

43
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,300
We promised it long ago.

44
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:32,840
I'll send you to the far
ends of the new world!

45
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,400
The G-G-Cannonball!

46
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,340
No more biscuits!

47
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:04,840
Oh, my God.

48
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,580
Excuse me, Mama.

49
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,979
Sweet General Smoothie has arrived!

50
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:39,960
Um... Wonderful!

51
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,537
Sweet General Katakuri should be
arriving any moment now as well!

52
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:45,450
Lovely!

53
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:46,897
This will be a real treat!

54
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:48,817
It's been ages since
everyone got together.

55
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,860
Uh, what about Cracker?

56
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:53,041
Shouldn't he be back home by now?

57
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:56,359
Soon, I'm sure, and with
Straw Hat's head is a gift!

58
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,000
Goodness, I can't wait!

59
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,430
Huh?

60
00:04:14,513 --> 00:04:15,343
Well, that's weird.

61
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,280
What happened?

62
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:36,380
What is it?

63
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,000
Big brother!

64
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,020
Look at this!

65
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,600
He's in terrible shape!

66
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,460
This is messed up.

67
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:52,897
Cracker's one of our sweet three generals.

68
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:55,274
I'm gonna kill whoever did this to him.

69
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,540
Where's the bastard?

70
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:59,411
Seems he came flying from pretty far away.

71
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,560
Must have been the seducing woods.

72
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,957
He was supposed to take care
of Straw Hat Luffy there.

73
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,805
Then you know what that means.

74
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,560
Straw Hat Luffy is still at large.

75
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:14,328
He's around here somewhere.

76
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:18,260
Put out an emergency alert!

77
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:26,560
We need to take shelter now! What? Why?

78
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,260
Sweet General Cracker got
beat by Straw Hat! No way!

79
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:48,580
Hey, are you alright?

80
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:49,841
That was insane.

81
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,620
I ate a lifetime's worth of biscuits.

82
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,937
Huh, looks like you're shrinking already.

83
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:59,820
Uh-huh, that's because fourth
gear uses a lot of energy.

84
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,280
So there you are.

85
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:07,220
Were you hiding in the bushes? Kind of.

86
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,777
I ran away so Cracker wouldn't murder me.

87
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:12,277
I thought you guys were
going to lose for sure.

88
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:14,037
They're blunt, don't you think?

89
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:17,120
Well, I mean, he's one of
the sweet three generals.

90
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:19,640
Well, it's fine.

91
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:26,980
That was scary, but... We won!

92
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:31,950
Woo!

93
00:06:32,033 --> 00:06:32,863
Huh?

94
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:36,160
Would I kill you guys to cheer?

95
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,282
We'd be one of Big Mom's
top fighters, after all!

96
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:40,730
I...

97
00:06:40,813 --> 00:06:42,040
I can't even move.

98
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:45,457
We've engaged in treachery most foul.

99
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:49,840
We helped the enemy, and now
General Cracker has lost.

100
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:53,637
Everyone in Totoland knows that Mama's

101
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:57,120
vivacard holds tremendous
power over us homies.

102
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:01,729
That's why she doesn't share
pieces of it to anyone anymore,

103
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:04,822
not even to the little
Sprouts in her own family.

104
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:08,720
So why do you have one? Oh, neat.

105
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:12,477
This thing is even more
valuable than I thought.

106
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:15,640
Listen, you're in much
worse trouble than before.

107
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:17,000
And why's that?

108
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:23,860
A while back, Sweet General
Snack got taken down, too.

109
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:30,660
Then Cracker's fleet painted the
sea black with their numbers,

110
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:33,720
and Linlin's fury summoned the storm.

111
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:41,717
The enemy ships, powerful as they were,
got torn to shreds in the blink of an eye.

112
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,740
A storm?

113
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,824
Linlin can command the
weather, quite literally.

114
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:47,277
She controls weather?

115
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,560
In her left hand, Zeus, a thunder cloud.

116
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,220
In her right hand,
Prometheus, a living sun.

117
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:01,392
Once her rage is awakened, there's
nothing in this world that can stop her.

118
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:03,740
In other words,

119
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:08,605
you better get the heck out of here before
she finds out what you did to her boy.

120
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:12,240
She can get as mad as
she wants. I don't care.

121
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,197
I'm the one who should be angry here.

122
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,720
I still can't get over what Saji did.

123
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:24,137
How could he leave without telling us why?

124
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:26,300
All we got was a dumb note.

125
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:31,437
It's my problem to solve.

126
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,740
I'll be back soon.

127
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,417
So give everybody my best.

128
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,297
Okay, we only made it this far.

129
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:43,777
Thanks to Pudding's map,
and we already lost Peckums.

130
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:47,557
We should have Sanji by now,
but nobody showed at the coast.

131
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:50,897
We don't know if it was a trap or
if something bad happened to them.

132
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:55,537
Then we got lost in the
forest, wasted time, fighting.

133
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:59,817
Once Sanji gets married, he'll
be part of Big Mom's crew,

134
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:01,665
and it'll be too late to help.

135
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:04,420
That means we gotta get moving.

136
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,000
Yeah, but when is the wedding?

137
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:12,377
Cracker said the Vinsmokes were headed
to some castle for the ceremony,

138
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:13,931
and that should be today.

139
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:15,778
It's still morning.

140
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:18,214
We might have enough time to stop them.

141
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,180
Time isn't the issue.

142
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,537
If you don't run away, you'll die.

143
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,160
Don't worry. Let's go!

144
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:34,780
Hey, Tree! Huh?

145
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:39,780
You know where the castle
is, don't you? I suppose.

146
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,197
Good, I need you to carry me there.

147
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,162
Nein, I refuse.

148
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:49,040
I won't quit. No way.

149
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,740
We're taking Soji back.

150
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:16,890
It's chopper.

151
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:19,200
How are you doing? Hanging in there.

152
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:23,654
We should be able to meet up with you
and Brooke if everything works out.

153
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:26,377
It doesn't sound like things
are working out at all.

154
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:29,897
You can't help us from outside the
mirror, so it's better not to worry.

155
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,357
Just keep going for...

156
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,840
Hey, Chopper!

157
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,897
Seriously, Nabi, everything's fine.

158
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,627
We're doing right over here.

159
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:38,648
Oh, everything's fine, huh?

160
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:42,657
At any rate, we'll keep heading to
the castle and hope we run into Sanji.

161
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:43,570
Sounds good.

162
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:47,585
Once you rescue him, use that
piece of the mirror to contact us.

163
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:48,860
It broke!

164
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,340
Hey, Chopper? Carrot?

165
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:54,120
It's a normal mirror now.

166
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:55,792
Oh, I hope they're okay.

167
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:00,650
Ah!

168
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,627
He's shrinking down already?

169
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,060
Whoa! What?

170
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:08,900
He's freaking me out!

171
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:12,080
No way!

172
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,620
I can't believe it!

173
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,428
He's almost back to normal!

174
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:20,020
The human body doesn't work like that!

175
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,380
Gimme meat! Meat?

176
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:25,400
Hey there, Fraulein!

177
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:28,560
You've got good luck. Why's that?

178
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,082
There they are.

179
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,200
That's German double six.

180
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:41,400
So is Sanji with them?

181
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,880
Yeah, look!

182
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,500
Hey! Sanji!

183
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:51,860
Your Majesty, something
is charging towards us.

184
00:11:56,380 --> 00:12:00,340
That idiot, he made it all
the way to whole cake island.

185
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,837
And what's with that tree?

186
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:04,937
It's running.

187
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:07,117
Hey, sanji!

188
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:11,817
We finally made it—I was
afraid we'd be too late.

189
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:14,377
But it looks like we're right on time.

190
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:16,697
What are they doing here?

191
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:18,577
This is bad—how amusing!

192
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:22,280
how amusing That's Straw Hat Luffy.

193
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:23,670
Hey!

194
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,000
He came here to pick you up!

195
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,965
You're gonna tip over
the calicoat, you maniac!

196
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:31,220
Come on, Sanji!

197
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:33,977
You said you'd be back,
but I didn't want to wait.

198
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:34,890
You know me.

199
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:39,780
Let's party!

200
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:46,157
I was gonna come alone, but
it turned into a whole thing.

201
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:48,557
You mentioned your hands
are important to you.

202
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:52,480
If you try to flee, your
hands will be blown off.

203
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:59,708
You know what happens
if you know Sholeiloh.

204
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:04,224
Zoro took a team and
headed to the land of Wano.

205
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,780
I won't hesitate to relieve
this man of his head.

206
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,773
So it's me, Brook, Nami, and
Chopper who came to get you.

207
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:15,902
You'll be a sacrifice for
the family, understood?

208
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:17,637
I haven't changed my opinion of you.

209
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,777
But as a man, if you ever
stray from the honorable path,

210
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:22,566
then I'll slit my own throat.

211
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,477
Sanji! I'm hungry!

212
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:28,031
And I do not think of you as a worthy son.

213
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:31,117
Because as a parent, I've
got to take responsibility.

214
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:33,612
Loving you as a son is my greatest shame.

215
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:38,740
Hey, Sanji.

216
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:42,780
Take care.

217
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,780
Don't catch cold.

218
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:49,160
I'll explain more back on the boat.

219
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,070
Sanji!

220
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,122
What the heck's gotten into you?

221
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:02,920
Leave my sight, bunch
of low-class pirates.

222
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:10,440
Make no mistake, I have
always been a Vinsmoke.

223
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,600
Which makes me a prince.

224
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,117
Of the Germa kingdom.

225
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,000
I kept all this a secret from you because,

226
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:21,426
knowing this would make
things harder for you.

227
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:26,687
But now that it's out, you can see there's
a clear difference in our standings.

228
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:29,197
If I stay here, I'll
have all the servants,

229
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,809
soldiers, and riches
I could ever dream of!

230
00:14:32,060 --> 00:14:34,357
So I can go back to that crappy ship with

231
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:37,028
you and your friends
on some dumb adventure!

232
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:40,077
Or I can stay right here
and marry the beautiful

233
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,689
daughter of a wealthy
and powerful emperor.

234
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:46,557
Now, which of those do you
think would make me happier?

235
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:47,797
Here, I'll spell it out.

236
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:50,537
I just wrote that note
to get you off my back.

237
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:52,240
I'm not going anywhere.

238
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:58,767
It's noble of you to come all the way
here to get me, but you wasted your time.

239
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,140
I'm not leaving.

240
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,421
I've already forgotten your name.

241
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,722
Yeah, whatever!

242
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:05,857
You big liar!

243
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:09,740
Think I'm gonna buy
that don't worry Sanji.

244
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,137
I'll help you drive them off.

245
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:12,050
Don't you dare

246
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,337
This one's mine.

247
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:17,740
I'll send him packing

248
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:32,840
What do you mean you'll send me packing
I want you to leave what else can I mean

249
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:39,064
Don't know why you thought
this was a good idea.

250
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:43,497
Couldn't have been easy to get here,
so I know you must want me back.

251
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:47,120
But having said that, if you
really value my happiness,

252
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:49,477
don't you have all this backwards?

253
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:50,390
Frankly,

254
00:15:50,473 --> 00:15:51,577
you guys are poor and weak,

255
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:56,484
especially compared to the Big Mom Pirates,
who are generous enough to take me in.

256
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,940
So why would I ever choose you?

257
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:02,089
These are the big leagues.

258
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:05,006
You being king of the
pirates is a pipe dream.

259
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:09,060
It's only human nature
to pick the winning side.

260
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,680
You think this is funny, Sanji?

261
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:14,215
Nothing you're saying makes any sense!

262
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,860
So we were never really friends?

263
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,440
You were fooling me all this time?

264
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:25,340
That's right. Sorry.

265
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:29,101
Never thought much of you at all.

266
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:35,480
Did he just summon a flame? No way!

267
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:39,700
I'm glad we got Frontier seats to this

268
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:44,960
Is it hard to accept I imagine
you two didn't see this coming

269
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,520
Then I'll prove it to you

270
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,040
Get ready

271
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,880
Now Diablo Jamba

272
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:02,400
Shoo shot

273
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:33,980
Luffy's bleeding.

274
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,080
It can't be.

275
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:37,780
Is Sanji serious?

276
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:44,400
I said get ready.

277
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:48,140
If you don't use your Haki, you'll die.

278
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,780
What do I need Haki for?

279
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,628
I just want to talk to you.

280
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:59,200
Do what you want.

281
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,740
I won't fight.

282
00:18:08,260 --> 00:18:12,080
You won't fight, then go away.

283
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:18,520
Not happening, you're stuck with me.

284
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:24,600
Selfish as usual, all right
then have it your way.

285
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,200
So listen, Mr.

286
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:47,438
Cook, why don't you leave
this boat and join my crew?

287
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:51,086
I could use a cook like
you on my pirate ship.

288
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:57,853
We don't want to fight, we want to help!

289
00:18:58,480 --> 00:18:59,580
Don't you get it?

290
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:04,748
Lock fought all night against one of Big
Mom's strongest generals to get here.

291
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:07,800
He's in no shape to do this.

292
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:08,920
Nami, cut it out.

293
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:11,600
Stay out of this, okay?

294
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,500
It's between us.

295
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:15,240
We're having a duel.

296
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:22,514
Oh, that's what you think this is, huh?

297
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,360
Sanji, no!

298
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,497
Get out of my way!

299
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:00,410
Right!

300
00:20:00,493 --> 00:20:01,500
I'm done with you!

301
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:08,960
That's enough!

302
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,580
Scram!

303
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,020
Beat it!

304
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,120
Go away!

305
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:43,460
I'm not leaving.

306
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:07,000
Oh, Lupi!

307
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,000
Don't do this!

308
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:44,040
Here we go.

309
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:02,040
How did this happen?

310
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:03,740
This is insane!

311
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:19,057
Please, Sanji, you don't
have to go through with this!

312
00:22:19,140 --> 00:22:21,022
We'll go, just don't hurt Luffy!

313
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:31,120
I'm not leaving!

314
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:36,680
You're a good cook and I need one!

315
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:39,193
Obviously we should be pirates together!

316
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,190
Kunkasee!

317
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:13,737
What amazing strength!

318
00:23:13,820 --> 00:23:16,840
I'd expect nothing less
if I've been smoke.

319
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:25,620
Please tell me you're
all right? Luffy! Luffy!

320
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:27,520
Come on, you gotta get up!

321
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:28,697
Say something to me!

322
00:23:28,780 --> 00:23:29,956
Tell me you're okay!

323
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:41,120
Hey, Sanji!

324
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:42,240
Not so fast!

325
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,360
Now we're through.

326
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:51,240
I'm sorry.

327
00:23:51,660 --> 00:23:53,260
Sorry we ever came here.

328
00:23:54,180 --> 00:23:55,960
Aw, damn, that is so hot.

329
00:23:56,180 --> 00:23:57,360
I like him, Feisty.

330
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,837
Their ties were meaningless.

331
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:10,300
Glad he severed them.

332
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,510
Thanks for waiting.

333
00:24:12,593 --> 00:24:13,423
Let's go.

334
00:24:14,100 --> 00:24:14,930
Yes, sir.

335
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:23,710
Luffy!

336
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:32,660
Come back!

337
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:34,870
Sanji!

338
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:44,120
All your excuses sounded so fake!

339
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:48,017
I don't know why you said that
crap, but I know you didn't mean it!

340
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:49,937
You think that's going to make me leave?

341
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:51,137
Like we aren't friends?

342
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:54,455
A couple of dumb lies won't
make me give up on my crew.

343
00:24:54,820 --> 00:24:56,232
What do you take me for?

344
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:58,140
I'm not stupid.

345
00:24:58,520 --> 00:24:59,932
I know what's happening.

346
00:25:01,340 --> 00:25:03,660
No matter how much you kick me,

347
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:07,360
you're the one who's getting hurt.

348
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:18,020
It's over.

349
00:25:18,240 --> 00:25:20,877
Luffy, for some reason, Sanji's done.

350
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:22,240
Just shut up!

351
00:25:23,420 --> 00:25:24,380
Should we stop?

352
00:25:24,620 --> 00:25:25,620
He's still there.

353
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:27,900
Keep going.

354
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:39,580
By the way, have you ever
heard of the All-Blue?

355
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,060
That sea is a genuine miracle!

356
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:43,640
It has it all!

357
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:50,300
We're not done yet!

358
00:25:50,760 --> 00:25:52,780
Our journey isn't over!

359
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:58,520
I'm staying right here and
I'm not moving an inch!

360
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:01,348
I'm gonna keep waiting
for you to come back!

361
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:05,920
And if you leave me here,
I'll just starve to death!

362
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,500
You're my chef!

363
00:26:08,860 --> 00:26:11,060
No one else can take your place!

364
00:26:11,860 --> 00:26:14,507
Sanji was making some
of that rat food again.

365
00:26:15,980 --> 00:26:20,140
I'm not eating another bite of
anything unless you cook it!

366
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:25,880
Even if I get hungry,

367
00:26:26,180 --> 00:26:32,720
even if spears or swords or stones break
down on me, I'll keep waiting for you!

368
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:50,717
you better come back you hear me no matter

369
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:56,280
what i need you on my
crew sanji without you

370
00:26:57,240 --> 00:27:01,880
without you i'll never
be king of the pirates
